@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How MontanaMesh Runs";
}

<section class="app-shell page-hero reveal" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open Stack / Public Services / Local Ingress</p>
    <h1 id="setup-title">How MontanaMesh runs.</h1>
    <p>
        The public website, dashboards, MQTT broker, and ingestion tools run as a small containerized stack with private management paths and public community-facing endpoints.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="app-shell platform-grid" aria-label="MontanaMesh hosting stack">
    <article class="platform-card reveal">
        <span class="card-index">Public VPS</span>
        <h2>Fedora 42 at RackNerd</h2>
        <p>The public stack runs from a Fedora VPS with Podman services behind Caddy.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Caddy:</strong> TLS and public routing.</li>
            <li><strong>ASP.NET Core:</strong> this website.</li>
            <li><strong>Mosquitto:</strong> MQTT broker for Meshtastic traffic.</li>
            <li><strong>MeshMonitor:</strong> public node map and dashboard.</li>
            <li><strong>PotatoMesh Web:</strong> ingestion API and map companion.</li>
            <li><strong>Portainer:</strong> private container management.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.racknerd.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RackNerd</a>
    </article>

    <article class="platform-card reveal">
        <span class="card-index">Private Link</span>
        <h2>Tailscale management</h2>
        <p>Tailscale keeps operator-only services off the public internet while still allowing remote administration and monitoring.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Private service dashboards.</li>
            <li>Host-to-host ingress paths.</li>
            <li>Remote maintenance without exposing admin ports.</li>
        </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="platform-card reveal">
        <span class="card-index">Local Ingress</span>
        <h2>Wormhole radio bridge</h2>
        <p>The Wormhole host connects local radio hardware back to the public services over the private link.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Host:</strong> Dell OptiPlex class machine.</li>
            <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> Podman user services.</li>
            <li><strong>Work:</strong> forwards node, position, telemetry, and message data into PotatoMesh.</li>
        </ul>
    </article>
</section>

